{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the beast you shall kill.</b> If a man sinned, what did the beast sin? Rather, because it brought stumbling to the man through itself, therefore Scripture says it shall be stoned — a fortiori for a man, who knows to distinguish between good and evil, yet causes evil to his fellow to transgress. So too you say: ״אַבֵּד תְּאַבְּדוּן אֶת כָּל הַמְּקֹמוֹת״ (Deuteronomy 12) — here is an a fortiori: if trees, which do not see and do not hear, because stumbling came through them the Torah said: destroy, burn, and consume — [one] who diverts his fellow from the path of life to the ways of death, how much the more so (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:26.762448711Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}